      "text": "Page 2\r\n\u2022 Education: online education companies sell courses directly to students.\r\nKey Characteristics:\r\n\u2022 Customers are individual consumers.\r\n\u2022 Transactions are generally smaller than B2B transactions.\r\n\u2022 Purchasing decisions can be influenced by price, convenience, brand and emotion.\r\n\u2022 Sales cycles are usually short.\r\n\u2022 Advertising, promotions, customer experience and after-sales service are important.\r\n4. C2C \u2013 Consumer to Consumer\r\nMeaning: C2C is a business model in which one individual consumer sells a product or service to another\r\nindividual consumer. An online marketplace or platform often connects the buyer and seller.\r\nSimple Example: Consumer A \u2192 Online Marketplace \u2192 Consumer B\r\nApplications:\r\n\u2022 Second-hand products: used phones, laptops, furniture, bicycles and other goods.\r\n\u2022 Online marketplaces: individuals list products for other individuals to purchase.\r\n\u2022 Auction platforms: consumers can sell products through bidding or auctions.\r\n\u2022 Classified advertisements: individuals advertise products or services for sale.\r\n\u2022 Ticket reselling: consumers may transfer or resell eligible tickets where permitted.\r\n\u2022 Rental platforms: individuals can offer assets or spaces to other individuals through a platform.\r\nKey Characteristics:\r\n\u2022 Both buyer and seller are consumers.\r\n\u2022 Online marketplaces commonly provide the platform.\r\n\u2022 Products may be new, used or second-hand depending on the marketplace.\r\n\u2022 Trust, ratings, reviews and seller reputation are important.\r\n\u2022 Price negotiation may be common.",
