      "text": "Page 3\r\n5. Difference Between B2B, B2C and C2C\r\nFeature B2B B2C C2C\r\nFull Form Business to Business Business to Consumer Consumer to Consumer\r\nSeller Business Business Individual consumer\r\nBuyer Business Individual consumer Individual consumer\r\nTypical Order Size Large Small/medium Small/medium\r\nTransaction Value Generally high Generally lower Varies\r\nDecision Basis ROI, efficiency, cost Price, convenience, experience Price, trust, condition\r\nSales Cycle Usually long Usually short Usually short\r\nNegotiation Common Less common Common\r\nRelationship Long-term Repeat or short-term Mostly transaction-based\r\nMarketing Professional/business marketing Mass and digital marketing Marketplace/reputation-based\r\nExample Supplier \u2192 Company Retailer \u2192 Customer Person \u2192 Person\r\n6. Real-Life Comparison Using a Laptop\r\nB2B: A company purchases 100 laptops for its employees.\r\nLaptop Manufacturer \u2192 Company\r\nB2C: An individual purchases one laptop for personal use.\r\nLaptop Retailer \u2192 Customer\r\nC2C: An individual sells a used laptop to another person through a marketplace.\r\nConsumer A \u2192 Marketplace \u2192 Consumer B\r\n7. Advantages\r\nB2B:\r\n\u2022 Large transaction values\r\n\u2022 Long-term customers\r\n\u2022 Repeat orders\r\n\u2022 Stable business relationships\r\nB2C:\r\n\u2022 Large customer market\r\n\u2022 Fast transactions\r\n\u2022 Direct customer feedback\r\n\u2022 Strong opportunities for digital marketing\r\nC2C:\r\n\u2022 Easy selling of unwanted products\r\n\u2022 Lower prices for buyers\r\n\u2022 Wide marketplace reach",
